Add native terminal self-archival

Threads cannot use Desktop archive tools while Desktop is closed.
Add `saffron.archive_self` for saved roots hosted by app-server.
An accepted call ends the requesting turn without another model request,
saving an optional `final_message` as the closing assistant response.
Further tool dispatch stops, active Code Mode cells terminate,
and the host receives archival only after successful turn persistence.
The `scheduled` receipt does not confirm that archival has completed.

Conditional shutdown rejects a request if newer work won admission.
Interruption and steering cancel pending requests, and a pending
handoff suppresses goal continuation without changing the goal status.
The host drains final notifications and uses native archival for storage
and spawned descendants; independent forks are unaffected.
Requests are transient and are not replayed after a server restart.
